Adapted work

Parts of Wayroost follow logic from Paseo (https://github.com/getpaseo/paseo),
Copyright (c) 2025-present Mohamed Boudra, licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0:

  * server/src/paseo/mirror.ts reconciles fetched history with live events
    using the same rules as the Paseo app's timeline sync (epoch/sequence
    gating, canonical catch-up, projected merging of streamed chunks and tool
    lifecycles).
  * server/src/paseo/normalize.ts builds answers to multi-question permission
    requests the way the Paseo app's question form does.

Parts of Wayroost are adapted from Hermes Agent
(https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent), Copyright (c) 2025 Nous
Research, licensed under the MIT License (reproduced below):

  * server/src/hermes/normalize.ts: skillInvocationText() is a port of
    apps/shared/src/skill-scaffold.ts. Its markers are copied byte for byte.
  * server/src/hermes/gateway.ts mirrors the JSON-RPC client behaviour of
    apps/shared/src/json-rpc-channel.ts and apps/shared/src/reconnect-backoff.ts:
    a fresh single-use ticket per connection, advertising server requests, the
    gateway.ping heartbeat, and jittered reconnects.

